    "description": "About Sarvam Sarvam is building the bedrock of Sovereign AI for India. The company is developing India's full-stack sovereign AI platform, building across research, models, infrastructure and applications with a singular focus on making AI genuinely work for India. Sarvam works with leading enterprises and public institutions and is backed by Lightspeed, Peak XV and Khosla Ventures. Sarvam partners with India's leading brands, including Tata Capital, SBI Life, CRED, IDFC and LIC. About the role Sarvam's model APIs (ASR, TTS, Vision, LLM, Translate) are how developers and enterprises ship products on our foundation models. The platform handles tens of millions of API calls every day, over HTTP and WebSockets, with metering, billing, prepaid wallets and rate-limiting all part of the same stack. We are hiring a Software Engineer to own major parts of this platform end to end, working closely with the Staff Engineer who leads its architecture. You will take an area such as speech to text pipeline,or text to speech pipeline, and be accountable for its reliability, performance and end-to-end latencies. This role is for someone who is obsessed with latencies, optimizes services and network paths to shave off milliseconds, ships fast, reasons from first principles, and treats AI as the default way to get engineering work done. What you will do Own a platform area end to end \u2022 Own one or more major parts of the platform, such as the WebSocket streaming layer, a speech recognition pipeline, or text to speech pipeline: build, operate and improve them. \u2022 Turn loosely defined goals into RFCs, milestones and shipped results, and write down the decisions and trade-offs. \u2022 Be accountable after launch: on-call, incident response, root-cause analysis and follow-through on fixes. \u2022 Make the call when a decision is needed, and own the outcome. \u2022 Obsessed with latencies, dissecting existing services to understand the system, and tuning the right knobs to optimize performance. \u2022 Bring services across without regressions in customer-facing APIs, latency or reliability. Build real-time and model-serving pipelines \u2022 Build and operate streaming infrastructure: WebSocket connections, long-lived sessions queue-based batch processing, backpressure and low-latency model invocation. \u2022 Engineer audio pipelines: TTS chunking around model context limits, sample-rate conversion and format encoding, and VAD-based silence detection for ASR. \u2022 Hold your services to sub-100ms latency SLOs in a multi-tenant environment, and know where every millisecond goes. Think in systems and from first principles \u2022 Reasons from constraints: latency budgets per hop, throughput, cost per request, failure modes and tenant isolation. \u2022 Use back-of-the-envelope estimates to decide what to build, what to optimize and what to leave alone. \u2022 Prefer simple designs you can fully explain over clever ones you cannot. \u2022 Build in observability from day one: logging, metrics and tracing that let anyone debug prod",
